    13	## §1. Composition Challenges
    14	
    15	A composition challenge says: build a single mathematical object whose
    16	*definition* uses two or more existing edges from EDGES.md, and whose
    17	*evaluator* produces a number you can compare to a baseline. Why this
    18	matters: edges are catalogued individually; their *interactions* are
    19	mostly unexplored. Composition is the cheapest source of genuinely new
    20	mathematical objects.
    21	
    22	**Discipline:** every composition target must produce code that runs.
    23	File under `experiments/constructions/<name>/`. Cite the edges by ID
    24	in `definition.md`. Failure mode is "duplicate of [composed-edge-X]"
    25	or "construction-incoherent" if the object isn't well-defined.
    26	
    27	### C1 — A⊕C₃ bisection × 0.537-bits invariant
    28	**Edges:** E1.6 + E1.5
