Session 70 complete. Built C1 (composition of E1.6 + E1.5) at `experiments/constructions/g_q_bisection_invariant/`:

**The construction.** `g_q : ℕ → 𝔽_q × 𝔽_q`, `g_q(x) = (A(x) mod q, C_3(x) mod q)` where `A(x) = (x − L(x))/2`, `C_3(x) = A(x) − π(x)`. Three pre-stated predictions tested at N = 2·10⁶ across q ∈ {2,3,5,7,11,13}; all three PASS.

**New deliverables.**
1. Per-component closed form `H(F mod q | F(x−1) mod q) = h_2(F(X)/X)` extends from π (S69) to A and C_3 — mechanism is universal for monotone Ω-stratified summatories. Worst |diff| 5·10⁻⁶ at X = 2·10⁶.
2. New joint closed form `H(g_q(x) | g_q(x−1)) = H_3(1−ρ_A, ρ_π, ρ_C3)` in regime q² ≪ π(X) — was nowhere in the project before.
3. q-stable strengthening of E1.6 marginal independence to q ≤ 13: I(A mod q ; C_3 mod q) ≤ 1.2·10⁻⁴ bits.

**Structural picture.** Each component carries asymptotically 1 bit/step (ρ_A, ρ_C3 → 1/2) while their integer difference π carries 0 bits/step (ρ_π → 0); marginal q-stable independence holds. Destructive-interference bisection, complementary to E1.4 / E2.6's smooth-vs-oscillatory bisection. No polylog opening (components are pseudorandom at full rate).

**Files.** Construction at `experiments/constructions/g_q_bisection_invariant/` (definition.md, py, results.md, data.json, log). Updates: EDGES.md (E1.5 + E1.6 annotations), NOVELTY_CHALLENGES.md (C1 marked BUILT), RESEARCH_AGENDA.md (Arc 4 milestone), CLOSED_PATHS.md (row 746), `archive/sessions/session70_c1_g_q_bisection.md`, `.run_state = 63`.
